---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TallyEmbed from "../components/TallyEmbed.astro";

/* Cities that are actually planned go here even before format and
   dates are confirmed — `when` stays honest ("Planned") until a real
   date exists. Workshops run in different formats (introductory
   sessions, deep-dives, multi-day intensives), so `body` should
   describe whichever format that entry ends up being, once known. */
const workshops = [
  {
    city: "Munich",
    when: "Planned",
    body: "Practitioner training in the Sociogram Method — format and dates to be confirmed. Taught in English and German.",
  },
  {
    city: "London",
    when: "Planned",
    body: "Practitioner training in the Sociogram Method — format and dates to be confirmed. Taught in English.",
  },
];

const supervision = [
  "You bring one stuck client case — anonymised, in your own notes.",
  "We build the sociogram together and locate the structural bottleneck.",
  "You leave with a diagnosis you can use in your next session, and the reasoning behind it.",
  "Recurring slots available for practitioners who want ongoing case consultation.",
];
---

<Layout
  theme="lab"
  title="For Coaches & Therapists | The Sociogram Method"
  description="Train in the Sociogram Method: practitioner workshops, referral partnership, and an open invitation to contribute to the research."
>
  {/* ===== HERO ===== */}
  <section class="glow-top relative overflow-hidden border-b border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x relative z-10 grid gap-12 py-24 md:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] md:items-center md:py-28">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">For coaches &amp; therapists</span>
        <h1 class="mt-6 text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.6rem)] font-bold">
          Give your clients a map instead of more shame.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg">
          Most clients who arrive stuck in dating are not lacking confidence or communication
          skills. They are living inside a social structure that produces too few real encounters.
          The Sociogram Method makes that structure visible — so you can diagnose it rather than
          guess at it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="#workshops" class="btn btn-primary">See the workshops</a>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">No certification required to use the method</span>
          <span class="pill">English &amp; German</span>
          <span class="pill">Munich &amp; London</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <figure class="app-photo">
          <img
            src="/images/photos/coupleb.webp"
            alt="A couple sitting close together in a café, with the Amoro sociogram and its scored nodes drawn over the scene"
            width="1000"
            height="563"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== WHY ===== */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr]">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why this matters in your practice</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">
          The client isn't failing. Their opportunity structure is.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal space-y-5 leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
        <p>
          When a client reports months of effort and no progress, the standard moves are to work on
          confidence, communication, attachment, or presentation. Sometimes that is right. Often the
          bottleneck sits earlier: their week produces almost no repeated, trusted contact, their
          ties are locked in one context, and nobody in their network is positioned to introduce
          them onward.
        </p>
        <p>
          Without a way to see that, the work becomes a search for a defect in the person — which is
          both inaccurate and quietly harmful. A sociogram relocates the problem to something
          external, concrete, and changeable. Clients tend to relax the moment they see it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[color:var(--text)]">
          The method is not proprietary and requires no licence to use. It is published, and you are
          welcome to apply it in your own practice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== BOOK ===== */}
  <section class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">The training manual</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">Ending Loneliness.</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
          The full method in written form — the theory, the mapping procedure, the bottleneck
          taxonomy, and the intervention logic. If you want to work this way without waiting for a
          workshop, the book is the complete text, and everything I teach live is built on it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/ending-loneliness" class="btn btn-primary">About the book</a>
          <a href="/scv-framework" class="btn btn-ghost">Read the science</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="section-figure reveal">
        <img
          src="/images/covers/ending-loneliness.png"
          alt="Ending Loneliness by Dr. Axel Schumacher"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== WORKSHOPS ===== */}
  <section id="workshops" class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Workshops</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">
          Workshops on the Sociogram Method, added as they're confirmed.
        </h2>
        <p class="lead mt-6">
          Different formats — introductory sessions, deep-dives, and multi-day intensives —
          teaching the method with live mapping on real (anonymised) cases. Find workshops below
          as they're set; once there's more information on one, it goes up here.
        </p>
      </div>

      {
        workshops.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
            {workshops.map((w) => (
              <div class="card p-7">
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">{w.city}</h3>
                  <span class="font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-[0.72rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">
                    {w.when}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">{w.body}</p>
                <p class="mt-5 text-[0.78rem] leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
                  Exact dates, venue, and pricing are not yet confirmed. Register interest and
                  you'll be told first, with no obligation.
                </p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        )
      }

      <div class="card mt-8 p-8 text-center md:p-10">
        <span class="chip">No fixed dates yet</span>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
          Nothing is scheduled yet — tell me a city or format that would work for you and I'll
          reach out first once a workshop is set.
        </p>
        <a href="#enquiry" class="btn btn-primary mt-6">Register your interest</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== SUPERVISION ===== */}
  {/* Hidden for now, not deleted — flip `false` to re-enable if case
      supervision comes back as an offer. */}
  {false && (
  <section id="supervision" class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Practitioner supervision</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">
          Bring me a case you're stuck on.
        </h2>
        <p class="lead mt-6">
          One-to-one case consultation for coaches and therapists. Not training in the abstract —
          structural diagnosis applied to a client you are actually working with.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="offer-grid">
        <div class="offer">
          <div>
            <h3 class="offer__name">Case consultation</h3>
            <p class="offer__promise">
              A 60-minute working session on one client's social structure.
            </p>
            <p class="offer__price">On enquiry</p>
            <p class="offer__note">
              Single sessions or a recurring slot. Practitioner rate — tell me your setting and
              caseload.
            </p>
            <a href="#enquiry" class="btn btn-primary">Request supervision</a>
          </div>
          <ul class="offer__list">
            {supervision.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="note-box">
        <h3>On confidentiality</h3>
        <p>
          Bring cases anonymised. I do not need your client's name, and a sociogram works perfectly
          well with initials or pseudonyms for every person in it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  )}

  {/* ===== RESEARCH + REFERRAL ===== */}
  <section class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Two open invitations</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">
          The evidence base gets built by practitioners.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="card p-7">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Contribute to the research</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
            If you use structural mapping in your practice, I would like to hear what you see:
            which bottleneck patterns recur, which interventions move them, and where the method
            fails. Contributing practitioners are credited by name in any resulting publication.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
            Submissions are anonymised case patterns only — never client-identifying data. A written
            consent and data-handling protocol is provided before anything is shared, and you can
            withdraw at any point.
          </p>
          <a href="#enquiry" class="link-underline mt-5 text-sm">Ask about contributing →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-7">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Refer, and be referred</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
            I regularly meet clients whose real bottleneck is therapeutic, relational, or somatic —
            outside my scope. I would rather send them to someone good than stretch past what I do.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
            If your practice covers ground mine doesn't, tell me what you do and who you're right
            for. Where the fit is genuine, referrals go both ways — no fees, no commission, no
            formal agreement.
          </p>
          <a href="#enquiry" class="link-underline mt-5 text-sm">Introduce your practice →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card mt-8 p-8 text-center md:p-10">
        <span class="chip">Coming soon</span>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-semibold">The sociogram intake template</h3>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
          The intake sheet I use to build a client sociogram in the first session — the questions,
          in order, with notes on what each one is actually measuring. Free for practitioners.
        </p>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
          Stay tuned.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== ENQUIRY ===== */}
  <section id="enquiry" class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Get in touch</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">Tell me about your practice.</h2>
        <p class="lead mt-6">
          Supervision, workshops, research, referrals — one form for all of it. Tell me which, and
          what you work on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card mt-10 p-8 md:p-12">
        <TallyEmbed formId="WOaOLJ" title="Coach & Practitioner Enquiry" height={1146} />
      </div>

      <div class="note-box">
        <h3>Where this is heading</h3>
        <p>
          A structured certification track for practitioners is in development, and will follow once
          the workshops have run and the material has been tested against real practice. Everyone on
          the workshop interest list hears about it first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
